# The chip update checks in the simulator (batch 5, sitting 4gh-b5):
# Developer > Bench session > Chip update checks, end to end, through the
# real menus (devbench.h bench_batch_picks).  pre, then s05 always (the
# stages with the stage 4 bench), s4b hands off, s4c and its question,
# the restart (boot) onto the display driver, the resident image's
# checks (jobs, the drift outside the session, vf0, jvpu), with sitting
# 4gh's VC rows whose answer batch 5 can change and the PP reruns
# (preg, pldo, p1, pcop, psrf, awlg, duty, and 4gh-b5's heap A/B; s1,
# vs, sd: all refused by
# the sim; l5, ck and vlong passed in 4gh and are cut), s6 and its
# question, then sdc: armed,
# a play from Videos outside the session (the first-use check, its CLOSE
# carrying SDRAM idle in the model), back, its question; sd last.  The
# end: each pick once, in order, the end line, b9bcbe57's verified
# line (b13 and b5 after jvpu, as in the re-verify run), the
# clock150 token line (s4c and s6 passed).
# Generated by scripts/bench_sim_script.py (batch); edit that, not this.
# needs: video
# golden: skip
# np: viz-full
# reset: viz
# env: SIM_VCHECK=1
# log: s05: stages
# log: s4b: stages
# log: s4c: stages
# log: vf0: PASS
# log: sdc: armed
# log: sdc: idle code 0 polls
# nolog: vlong:
# log: s1: Not run (sim)
# log: sd: Not run (sim)
# log: heap: Not run (sim)
# log: heap walk at=<jobs
# log: heap walk at=>sd
# nolog: heap BAD
# log: unit check: token dropped (bench reset)
# nolog: glass owned STALE
# nolog: bench_sim: watchdog
# timeout: 300
wait 4000
bench_sim reset          # no results files, the model's defaults
copy ../../bcmfw/video/vcheck.bin /.rockbox/vcheck.bin
rm_file /.rockbox/.sim_vcheck_band
rm_file /.rockbox/.sim_vcheck_bad
video_start /Misc/S01E03.m4v   # this unit's check result
wait 4000
video_stop
wait 500
wheel +20 40            # the last row (Now Playing while music plays)
wait 400
wheel -1 200            # Settings
wait 400
key SELECT
wait 1200
key SELECT              # About
wait 1500
chord SELECT+LEFT 3200  # Developer
wait 1000
wheel +1 200            # Bench session
wait 400
key SELECT
wait 1200
wheel +40 10          # Chip update checks
wait 400
key SELECT
wait 800
wheel +40 10          # the confirm screen: start
wait 400
key SELECT
wait 800
# -- preg: hands off (refused by the sim)
wheel +40 10          # Hands off now (preg)
wait 400
key SELECT
wait 800
wheel +40 10          # Automatic checks done (preg)
wait 400
key SELECT
wait 800
# -- s05: the test pictures and the stage 4 bench (always)
wheel +40 10          # Test pictures: start
wait 400
key SELECT
wait 800
wheel +40 10          # s05: Yes
wait 400
wheel -3 200
wait 400
key SELECT
wait 800
# -- s4b: hands off
wheel +40 10          # Hands off now (s4b)
wait 400
key SELECT
wait 800
wheel +40 10          # Automatic checks done
wait 400
key SELECT
wait 800
# -- s4c
wheel +40 10          # Fast clock pictures: start
wait 400
key SELECT
wait 800
wheel +40 10          # s4c: Yes
wait 400
wheel -3 200
wait 400
key SELECT
wait 800
# -- boot (Display program): the restart
wheel +40 10          # Display program: start
wait 400
key SELECT
wait 800
wheel +40 10          # Now restart: close
wait 400
key SELECT
wait 800
key LEFT                # the stopped-session screen: leave
wait 800
reboot
wait 4000
